in chief of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, suggesting that American=
 and Iranian officials meet soon.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25=
px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Initially, the proposal =
seemed well received, and officials from Qatar, Pakistan, Turkey and Saudi =
Arabia have all been involved in communicating with the Iranians. But in re=
cent days, some American negotiators have turned more pessimistic, accordin=
g to people familiar with their thinking, fearing that whatever agreement t=
hey reach could be undercut back in Tehran by radical hard-liners.</span></=
p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15p=
x"><span>History shows that a diplomatic solution is the only way to have l=
